{"id": "EUVD-2026-92025", "enisaUuid": "b8d76043-c662-3631-8a0c-68afb288c97a", "description": "OpenAM before 16.1.3 contains an improper authorization vulnerability that allows delegated administrators to destroy sessions outside their realms because realm checks use the requester's realm. Authenticated accounts holding the iplanet-am-session-destroy-sessions attribute can supply a target session identifier or handle to forcibly log out users in any realm.", "datePublished": "2026-10-03T12:14:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-05T20:29:43", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/OpenIdentityPlatform/OpenAM/security/advisories/GHSA-hmwh-9r8r-44gw", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openam-before-16.1.3-improper-authorization-in-delegated-session-destroy-realm-scoping"], "aliases": ["GHSA-86x4-hjp8-8h99", "CVE-2026-105121"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ca2437dc-10d0-3256-8c01-9b7fb5af2007", "product": {"name": "OpenAM", "vendor": {"name": "OpenIdentityPlatform"}}, "product_version": "0 <16.1.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "449c067c-5b01-3a29-b34d-40cc36cd6216", "vendor": {"name": "OpenIdentityPlatform"}}], "isExploited": false}